{"name":"get_unifi_placement_snapshot","title":"Get UniFi Placement Snapshot","description":"Return a bounded, read-only UniFi topology and placement projection (unifi.placement-snapshot/v1). Unlike other tools' whole upstream bodies, this closed schema selects, renames and derives fields (a MAC-only device gets a SHA-256 source_id, withheld under redaction; device_type is a closed enum). Sources (GET only): InnerSpace 3D placement, Protect cameras/sensors, Site Manager inventory; no connector writes. Provenance has a 120-second freshness contract.

Returns schema_version, generated_at, freshness, provenance, floors, walls, placed_devices, topology, placement_links, plus incomplete/incompleteReason if a source list stops short. Address/asset fields (ip/mac, floor image/model/zip/bin URLs) are included by default; only opt-in UNIFI_REDACT_SECRETS removes them and URL/IP/MAC/credential strings, counting each in _withheld (section.field/reason) with _withheld_how_to_obtain naming the source tool (both absent with redaction off). Records outside schema v1 (not_an_object, no_position, no_geometry, no_source_id, not_numeric) are counted in _unprojected with _unprojected_how_to_obtain. Duplicate Network devices merge onto Protect nodes (Network-only fields omitted). For full payloads use get_innerspace_project, list_innerspace_devices, list_cameras, list_sensors or list_devices. Reference: docs/TOOL-USAGE.md#get_unifi_placement_snapshot.

Required arguments: host.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"host":{"type":"string","description":"Console name (case-insensitive reportedState.hostname/name, e.g. "my-console") or data[].id (MAC:numericId), from list_hosts. Serves Network and Protect."}},"required":["host"],"type":"object"},"outputSchema":{"additionalProperties":true,"properties":{"schema_version":{"description":"Snapshot schema id: unifi.placement-snapshot/v1.","type":"string"},"generated_at":{"description":"When the snapshot was built (ISO 8601 UTC).","type":"string"},"freshness":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Freshness contract: observed_at, max_age_seconds and cache.","type":"object"},"provenance":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Producer, approved read sources and read_only.","type":"object"},"floors":{"description":"Floor plans with their scale and map.","items":{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"walls":{"description":"Wall segments placed on floors.","items":{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"placed_devices":{"description":"Devices placed on floors, with positions.","items":{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"topology":{"description":"Network and Protect device inventory.","items":{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"placement_links":{"description":"Links from placed devices to inventory records by unique name.","items":{"additionalProperties":true,"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"incomplete":{"description":"True when a source list stopped short (opt-in page cap, repeated cursor).","type":"boolean"},"incompleteReason":{"description":"Why the result is incomplete, one reason per source; absent when complete.","type":"string"},"_unprojected":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Count of source records schema v1 cannot represent.","type":"object"},"_unprojected_how_to_obtain":{"description":"Which full read tool returns the unprojected records."},"_withheld":{"additionalProperties":true,"description":"Values removed under UNIFI_REDACT_SECRETS, counted.","type":"object"},"_withheld_how_to_obtain":{"description":"Which tool returns the withheld values, or how to disable redaction."}},"required":["schema_version","generated_at","freshness","provenance","floors","walls","placed_devices","topology","placement_links"],"type":"object"},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true},"_meta":{"unifi/apiSource":"innerspace/private/read","fastmcp":{"tags":[]}}}

